1
00:00:03,431 --> 00:00:03,431
[Intro]

2
00:00:03,431 --> 00:00:03,431
[Spoken, deadpan, over a single pulsing synth]

3
00:00:03,431 --> 00:00:06,782
Shot four-oh-one-one-seven.

4
00:00:06,782 --> 00:00:10,133
Plasma current ramping.

5
00:00:10,133 --> 00:00:11,729
Everybody look busy.

6
00:00:11,729 --> 00:00:11,729
[Verse 1]

7
00:00:11,729 --> 00:00:15,080
Back in fifty-eight they swore that it was nearly done

8
00:00:15,080 --> 00:00:18,670
Said we'd have it by the time their kids were twenty-one

9
00:00:18,670 --> 00:00:22,660
Now those kids have grandkids, still running the same plan

10
00:00:22,660 --> 00:00:26,489
With a plasma like a cat that will escape you if it can

11
00:00:26,489 --> 00:00:30,239
So I did the math on a whole career of mine

12
00:00:30,239 --> 00:00:34,149
Writing papers for a reactor I won't see come online

13
00:00:34,149 --> 00:00:34,149
[Pre-Chorus]

14
00:00:34,149 --> 00:00:37,979
Every decade there's a graph going up and to the right

15
00:00:37,979 --> 00:00:45,798
Every startup's got a deck that says we're turning on tonight

16
00:00:45,798 --> 00:00:45,798
(Series A, Series B, net electricity by twenty-three)

17
00:00:45,798 --> 00:00:45,798
[Chorus]

18
00:00:45,798 --> 00:00:49,707
It's thirty years away (thirty years away)

19
00:00:49,707 --> 00:00:52,899
Every time I check, it's thirty years away

20
00:00:52,899 --> 00:00:56,649
We got net gain! (if you don't count the wall plug)

21
00:00:56,649 --> 00:01:00,080
We got ignition! (for a billionth of a second)

22
00:01:00,080 --> 00:01:04,309
Funding's in the mail and en-ess-tee-ex-you broke again

23
00:01:04,309 --> 00:01:14,309
It's thirty years away, and it's thirty years away

24
00:01:15,798 --> 00:01:15,798
[Verse 2]

25
00:01:15,798 --> 00:01:19,548
Fourteen em-ee-vee neutrons, they don't care about your steel

26
00:01:19,548 --> 00:01:23,218
Fifty dee-pee-ay later, does your first wall still feel real

27
00:01:23,218 --> 00:01:27,128
The world's whole stash of tritium weighs about as much as my dog

28
00:01:27,128 --> 00:01:30,957
And it's half gone in twelve years while we're stuck in the backlog

29
00:01:30,957 --> 00:01:34,707
The divertor eats ten megawatts per square meter, give or take

30
00:01:34,707 --> 00:01:38,617
That's a rocket nozzle running every hour you're awake

31
00:01:38,617 --> 00:01:38,617
[Pre-Chorus]

32
00:01:38,617 --> 00:01:42,606
Disruption! Runaway electrons drilling through the tile

33
00:01:42,606 --> 00:01:50,505
ELM crash! Fifty times a second, take it with a smile

34
00:01:50,505 --> 00:01:50,505
(Breed it, shield it, cool it, heal it, then compete with pee-vee)

35
00:01:50,505 --> 00:01:50,505
[Chorus]

36
00:01:50,505 --> 00:01:54,415
It's thirty years away (thirty years away)

37
00:01:54,415 --> 00:01:57,606
Every time I check, it's thirty years away

38
00:01:57,606 --> 00:02:01,356
We got net gain! (if you don't count the wall plug)

39
00:02:01,356 --> 00:02:04,707
We got ignition! (for a billionth of a second)

40
00:02:04,707 --> 00:02:08,378
Funding's in the mail and the magnet just quenched

41
00:02:08,378 --> 00:02:17,074
It's thirty years away, and it's thirty years away

42
00:02:17,074 --> 00:02:17,074
[Verse 3]

43
00:02:17,074 --> 00:02:17,074
[Faster, half-rapped, tight drums]

44
00:02:17,074 --> 00:02:20,426
Got a grant to build a framework that would unify the codes

45
00:02:20,426 --> 00:02:24,016
Now there's fifteen of those frameworks and a sixteenth on the road

46
00:02:24,016 --> 00:02:28,005
It's got a logo, it's got a website, it's got a workshop every spring

47
00:02:28,005 --> 00:02:32,473
Got a slide that says "adopted," but nobody runs the thing

48
00:02:32,473 --> 00:02:36,064
Quarterly report says every milestone's in the green

49
00:02:36,064 --> 00:02:39,654
Signed and stamped and forwarded to folks you've never seen

50
00:02:39,654 --> 00:02:43,245
Program manager, office director, all the way to DC

51
00:02:43,245 --> 00:02:47,793
A mile-long trail of success for a repo with two stars (and one of them is me)

52
00:02:47,793 --> 00:02:47,793
(Deliverable met! Impact: transformational!)

53
00:02:47,793 --> 00:02:47,793
(Last commit: twenty twenty-one, documentation: aspirational)

54
00:02:47,793 --> 00:02:47,793
[Verse 4]

55
00:02:47,793 --> 00:02:47,793
[Sung, sneering]

56
00:02:47,793 --> 00:02:54,894
Founder wants a proposal, then a better one, then three

57
00:02:54,894 --> 00:02:58,324
Every draft a new objection, "we'll get to equity"

58
00:02:58,324 --> 00:03:02,154
Once the good ideas are on paper, all that talk just disappears

59
00:03:02,154 --> 00:03:06,543
"Let's collaborate through the university!" (Same work. Zero pay. Cheers.)

60
00:03:06,543 --> 00:03:09,973
Want my time? You email my supervisor, never me

61
00:03:09,973 --> 00:03:13,803
Want your name on my paper for the data that was free

62
00:03:13,803 --> 00:03:13,803
[Pre-Chorus]

63
00:03:13,803 --> 00:03:17,553
Opportunity! Weekly meetings and it doesn't pay

64
00:03:17,553 --> 00:03:21,303
Privilege! Thirty K, the rent's thirty-two, hooray

65
00:03:21,303 --> 00:03:21,303
(Saving the planet, guarding turf, and calling bad work "rude")

66
00:03:21,303 --> 00:03:21,303
[Chorus]

67
00:03:21,303 --> 00:03:29,202
It's thirty years away (thirty years away)

68
00:03:29,202 --> 00:03:32,473
Funding's in the mail, but could you do it for free?

69
00:03:32,473 --> 00:03:40,532
It's thirty years away, and it's thirty years away

70
00:03:40,532 --> 00:03:40,532
[Bridge]

71
00:03:40,532 --> 00:03:40,532
[Half-time, moody]

72
00:03:40,532 --> 00:03:44,282
In seventy-six they drew a chart, one line was labeled "never"

73
00:03:44,282 --> 00:03:47,793
They funded us below that line, then asked what took forever

74
00:03:47,793 --> 00:03:51,383
So I ran the integrated model and the model says it's fine

75
00:03:51,383 --> 00:03:55,372
Research ops in thirty-four, dee-tee in thirty-nine

76
00:03:55,372 --> 00:03:58,883
Six months to set it up, two years to get in print

77
00:03:58,883 --> 00:04:02,553
Validated on a reactor that doesn't yet exist

78
00:04:02,553 --> 00:04:06,941
It's a neural net surrogate trained on a code that's way too slow

79
00:04:06,941 --> 00:04:10,532
A model of a model of a plasma we don't know

80
00:04:10,532 --> 00:04:12,048
But the plots...

81
00:04:12,048 --> 00:04:12,048
(look good to me)

82
00:04:12,048 --> 00:04:13,484
The plots...

83
00:04:13,484 --> 00:04:13,484
(look good to me)

84
00:04:13,484 --> 00:04:13,484
[Breakdown]

85
00:04:13,484 --> 00:04:13,484
[Spoken, drums only]

86
00:04:13,484 --> 00:04:21,463
Reviewer one says: this paper is terrible if you don't cite my "very impactful" work. (No further comments.)

87
00:04:21,463 --> 00:04:24,415
Reviewer two says: please address the neutrons.

88
00:04:24,415 --> 00:04:28,564
Program office says: please put the framework on the highlights slide.

89
00:04:28,564 --> 00:04:31,835
Reviewer three says: have you considered more magnet.

90
00:04:31,835 --> 00:04:36,622
Startup keynote says: our novel framing. (That was my framing.)

91
00:04:36,622 --> 00:04:36,622
[Bass creeps back in]

92
00:04:36,622 --> 00:04:41,090
New proposal says: digital twin of the reactor. (There is no reactor.)

93
00:04:41,090 --> 00:04:45,559
Read-me says: real-time digital twin. Runtime: three weeks.

94
00:04:45,559 --> 00:04:49,548
Funding agency says: does it say digital twin? ...Funded.

95
00:04:49,548 --> 00:04:52,420
Solar says: we shipped while you were in review.

96
00:04:52,420 --> 00:04:55,771
Note to self: you built a framework too.

97
00:04:55,771 --> 00:04:57,846
Approved. Ship the reactor.

98
00:04:57,846 --> 00:04:57,846
[Final Chorus]

99
00:04:57,846 --> 00:04:57,846
[Key change up, full gang vocals]

100
00:04:57,846 --> 00:05:01,596
It's thirty years away (thirty years away)

101
00:05:01,596 --> 00:05:04,867
My advisor said it, and his advisor said the same

102
00:05:04,867 --> 00:05:08,697
We got net gain! (if you don't count the wall plug)

103
00:05:08,697 --> 00:05:12,048
We got ignition! (for a billionth of a second)

104
00:05:12,048 --> 00:05:15,559
The tokamak's a donut and the donut's always late

105
00:05:15,559 --> 00:05:20,106
It's thirty years away, so hey, I guess we wait

106
00:05:20,106 --> 00:05:20,106
[Outro]

107
00:05:20,106 --> 00:05:20,106
[Drops to a single synth]

108
00:05:20,106 --> 00:05:23,777
See you in thirty years.

109
00:05:23,777 --> 00:05:26,090
...make it thirty-five.

110
00:05:26,090 --> 00:05:28,963
...actually, don't wait up.

111
00:05:28,963 --> 00:05:32,473
I'll be on a bench, building a robot.

112
00:05:32,473 --> 00:05:35,186
It works, or it doesn't.

113
00:05:35,186 --> 00:05:36,144
And I'll know by lunch.

114
00:05:36,144 --> 00:05:41,500
[End]

